<xml>
  <block type="device_stepper_coils" x="30" y="30">
    <mutation uid="coils30" />
    <field name="NAME">motor</field>
    <field name="IN1">8</field>
    <field name="IN2">9</field>
    <field name="IN3">10</field>
    <field name="IN4">11</field>
    <field name="SPEED">500</field>
    <field name="ACCEL">100</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Purpose: Use one named 28BYJ-48 motor to travel between two positions with acceleration. Call run continuously; no delay interrupts the coil sequence.
Wiring: 28BYJ-48 + ULN2003: IN1 D8, IN2 D9, IN3 D10, IN4 D11. Common GND; use each module’s required supply.
Try: Change target 512 to 256 half-steps or reduce maximum speed and acceleration.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="510" y="30">
    <field name="VAR">target</field>
    <field name="TYPE">int32_t</field>
    <value name="VALUE">
      <block type="math_number">
        <field name="NUM">512</field>
      </block>
    </value>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="990" y="30">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="device_stepper_move">
        <field name="DEVICE">coils30</field>
        <field name="MODE">TO</field>
        <value name="VALUE">
          <block type="variables_get">
            <field name="VAR">target</field>
          </block>
        </value>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Set the first absolute target. This only requests movement; loop must service it.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="30" y="290">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="device_stepper_run">
        <field name="DEVICE">coils30</field>
        <next>
          <block type="controls_if">
            <value name="IF0">
              <block type="logic_compare">
                <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                <value name="A">
                  <block type="device_stepper_position">
                    <field name="DEVICE">coils30</field>
                    <field name="READ">DISTANCE</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="B">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">0</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
              </block>
            </value>
            <statement name="DO0">
              <block type="variables_set">
                <field name="VAR">target</field>
                <value name="VALUE">
                  <block type="math_arithmetic">
                    <field name="OP">MINUS</field>
                    <value name="A">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">0</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="B">
                      <block type="variables_get">
                        <field name="VAR">target</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <next>
                  <block type="device_stepper_move">
                    <field name="DEVICE">coils30</field>
                    <field name="MODE">TO</field>
                    <value name="VALUE">
                      <block type="variables_get">
                        <field name="VAR">target</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </next>
              </block>
            </statement>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Call run on every pass. At each target, reverse to the other position with acceleration and deceleration. No delay or slow display writes here; those would interrupt software pulse generation.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
